{
  "id": "ss.relic.biggame",
  "name": "Trophy jaw",
  "description": "One lower jaw, whole, stood on a small block of dark timber the way a trophy is mounted: the chin at the left, the body running right with five uneven teeth standing up along it, the front one the biggest,, and the ramus rising at the back as a tall stump. Pale bone with a darker band along the underside and a darker still facet on the rising branch, so it is a thick object with a side rather than a flat cutout. The relic is extra damage against the big ones, and the thing you keep from a big one is its jaw; the plinth is what says it was kept, and it is kept small so the bone is the object. There is one jaw and it is at rest, which separates it from the single moving mandible of ss.relic.execute.",
